WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.085
Last month, Liverpool star Lewis Diaz

00:00:02.085 --> 00:00:03.503
and his family suffered

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.131
the trauma of his father being kidnaped

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:07.924
and held hostage for 12 days

00:00:07.924 --> 00:00:09.342
by rebel Colombian

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:12.345
left wing organization, the L.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.888
One person who reached out to him

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:14.806
at the time

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:17.600
was former Chelsea and Nigeria star Mikel

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.228
John Obi. Incredibly, frighteningly.

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:21.521
His father was kidnaped

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.816
not once but twice during his career.

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:26.234
And he's been telling CNN's senior

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:30.363
sport analyst Darren Lewis about it.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:32.032
Because I saw you talked

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.241
about empathizing

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:34.325
with Lewis Diaz

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:36.536
after his father was kidnaped.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.205
Your father, Michael, was kidnaped twice.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.165
Can you talk us through

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:41.499
what happened the first time?

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:42.876
Yeah, He finished work

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:46.379
and he was going home, driving home

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:47.338
with his driver.

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:48.465
And, you know, they pulled

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.591
they got pulled over.

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:50.925
They got pulled over a car,

00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:51.926
went in front of them.

00:00:51.926 --> 00:00:53.511
They they got pulled over.

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:56.181
And yeah, he was taken

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:56.848
I think he was

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:59.851
taken for about ten days.

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:01.644
And and that's when, you know,

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:02.937
we're trying to.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.272
Started making phone calls

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:05.982
and they got in touch with us.

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:07.776
Obviously, they wanted to speak with me.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:10.028
So

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:11.905
so I spoke with them.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.074
They made their demands.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.241
I spoke to the club.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.618
I spoke to Roman.

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:17.869
Michael, what were their demands?

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:20.413
And the demands?

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:20.997
Demands sought

00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:23.458
to pay a huge amount of money.

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.710
You know that if I don't pay,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.713
my dad will not be released.

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:30.006
That they're going to shoot my dad.

00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:32.634
They're going to kill him if I don't pay.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.053
They know I have the money.

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:36.805
So if I want to see my dad again,

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:38.223
I have to make sure that I,

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:41.059
that I, that I bring the money.

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:41.768
I did speak

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:45.563
to the club, and Roman offered his help.

00:01:45.563 --> 00:01:48.191
If you need me to. To to do anything.

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:49.234
If you need me to get

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:51.986
to send my people over to Nigeria

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:53.947
to find your dad,

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.241
I'd be willing to do that.

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:57.909
You know, you have that option.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.327
But if you think you,

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:00.078
you, you,

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:01.496
you will pay the money, then you do.

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:04.874
So I finally had to pay the money.

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:07.377
And then my dad got released. Yeah.

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:08.586
And that was the first time. Yeah.

00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:09.629
So that was heartbreak.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.548
That was a heartbreaking moment.

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:12.632
To be reunited.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.592
What would that have been like?

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:15.426
Oh, that was.

00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:16.344
Yeah, Yeah. No.

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:17.887
Yeah, No, that was tough.

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:18.429
You know,

00:02:18.429 --> 00:02:21.307
See your dad come out, come out.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.393
You know, picture that up from from,

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:24.519
you know, from the street.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:26.062
You know, where he was dumped.

00:02:26.062 --> 00:02:27.689
And they tell you, go there and pick up

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:30.817
your dad like it's a trash, you know,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.195
bruised, beaten up

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:35.196
lips broken

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.574
everywhere, had swollen,

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:38.825
you know, things like that.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:41.411
Can't walk, can't move.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:44.205
It was a very heartbreaking moment for me

00:02:44.205 --> 00:02:44.998
and my family.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.124
So for me,

00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:49.294
when it happened again the second time,

00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:50.962
you know, it was even harder.

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:52.964
It was even much, much

00:02:52.964 --> 00:02:54.007
difficult to deal with.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:57.010
How did it happen the second time?

00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:57.510
A second

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.469
time was obviously

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:01.389
I was with the national team

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:02.891
at the World Cup 2018.

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:05.643
We're about to play against Argentina

00:03:05.643 --> 00:03:08.354
in the knockout stages,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.398
you know, just as everybody else.

00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:11.232
I was excited

00:03:11.232 --> 00:03:12.275
that, you know,

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:13.776
going into one of the biggest game

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:14.319
of my

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:15.445
of my life, playing

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:17.363
against Massey Energy and TNA,

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.573
I remember speaking to my mom

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:19.240
before the game.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:19.657
She was like,

00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:21.159
no, you can go out and perform.

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.285
You can't.

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:23.244
You're not in the right.

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:26.748
You can't perform, you can't play.

00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:28.333
I was like, Mom, I'm the captain.

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:28.958
I'm the leader.

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:29.918
I have to go out there

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:31.085
and show a bit of strength.

00:03:31.085 --> 00:03:32.712
I have to go out there, be strong.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.214
And that's exactly what I did.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.715
And unfortunately,

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.051
we didn't win the game.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.720
But yeah, I remember a few times

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.888
I thought I was going to.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.306
I thought I was going to show up.

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:44.474
I thought I was going to fall down

00:03:44.474 --> 00:03:46.893
and probably collapse or something.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.561
So when that happened to Diaz,

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.562
I definitely knew

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.563
what he was going through

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.649
as somebody who's been in that situation.

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:54.025
And that's why I reached out

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:55.443
and I showed my support

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:57.779
because I definitely knew

00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:59.781
exactly how he was feeling.

00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:01.908
You said that you reached out to Luis.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.159
Are you able to give us

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.536
any kind of insight into the conversation

00:04:05.536 --> 00:04:07.121
that you had.

00:04:07.205 --> 00:04:08.206
No idea really have a

00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:09.165
conversation with him?

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:10.291
I just you know, obviously,

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:11.376
I just showed my support,

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:11.626
you know,

00:04:11.626 --> 00:04:13.044
my support on social media

00:04:13.044 --> 00:04:14.629
saying how, you know, what I

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:16.005
you know, how I feel.

00:04:16.005 --> 00:04:17.131
And and

00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:18.549
I definitely know

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:21.552
exactly what he's going through.

00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:22.887
You know, it's a difficult moment.

00:04:22.887 --> 00:04:24.305
Again, I have to,

00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:27.517
you know, commend him and Liverpool,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.227
I can always say

00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.561
when you in this situations

00:04:30.561 --> 00:04:31.688
you need people around

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:33.273
you need people who care about you.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.400
And Liverpool showed their support.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.151
And I'm happy to see that

00:04:37.151 --> 00:04:40.488
that's what he got with Liverpool and

00:04:40.571 --> 00:04:41.614
and eventually,

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.324
you know, he's that finally got released.

